# Unleash (CR 702.98a): the restriction lasts only as long as it has a +1/+1 counter. Bot1 casts Dead Reveler and accepts
# the counter (it can't block). On turn 3 it attacks and Bot2's Scuzzback Scrapper blocks: the Scrapper's wither damage
# is dealt as a -1/-1 counter (CR 702.80a), which cancels the +1/+1 counter (CR 704.5q). With none left, the Reveler is a
# 2/3 again and no longer can't block.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Dead Reveler
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Scuzzback Scrapper
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Dead Reveler.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Keywords = CantBlock
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Scuzzback Scrapper.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Dead Reveler > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Scuzzback Scrapper > Dead Reveler)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Scuzzback Scrapper
Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Dead Reveler.Keywords = (absent)
